<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs - Friday actual 117,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs - Friday actual 117,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Actual interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog marketings Friday were 117,000 head, compared with the estimate of 110,000, according to USDA.</p>
<p>Saturday's actual receipts were 15,000 head, which matched the estimate. Opening trade was not well established. Early sales of Barrows and Gilts were $1.00 per cwt lower than the midsession Friday.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    52.00 -53.00	   53.00 -54.00</p>
<p>few			51.50  53.50	   52.50  54.50</p>
<p>Sows:  Steady to $2.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  42.00 -43.00	   42.50 -44.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -47.00	   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    48.00 -50.00	   49.00 -51.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
